WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.770
<i>Wealth, fame, power...</i>

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.670
<i>Gold Roger,
the King of the Pirates,</i>

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.970
<i>attained everything
this world has to offer.</i>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.840
<i>The words he uttered just before
his death drove people to the seas.</i>

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.680
<i>My treasure? If you want it,
you can have it!</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>Find it! I left everything
this world has to offer there!</i>

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.590
<i>And so men head for the Grand Line
in pursuit of their dreams!</i>

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.490
<i>The world has truly entered
a Great Pirate Era!</i>

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.860
<i>We're going to gather up
all our dreams</i>

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.770
<i>and set out in search
of something to find</i>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>ONE PIECE!</i>

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.620
<i>Compasses only cause delays</i>

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.350
<i>Delirious with fever,
I take the helm</i>

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:10.350
<i>If the dusty treasure map has
been verified, it's not a legend!</i>

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:18.170
<i>When it comes to personal storms,</i>

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.480
<i>simply ride aboard
someone else's biorhythm</i>

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.150
<i>and pretend it isn't there!</i>

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:32.650
<i>We're going to gather up
all our dreams</i>

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:38.360
<i>and set out in search
of something to find</i>

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:44.600
<i>A coin in my pocket,
and do you wanna be my friend?</i>

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.970
<i>We are, We are on the cruise!</i>

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.040
<i>We are!</i>

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.980
Here, Ghin. Let him eat it.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.320
<i>Sanji-san...</i>

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.650
Thank you!

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.670
This is a good restaurant.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.000
I'll take this ship.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:28.680
So... that's what you want...

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.010
Meat Ball of Doom!!

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.520
You're damn annoying!!

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.030
Don't defy me!

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.740
When I tell you to prepare food,

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.710
all you have to do is
obediently follow orders!

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.140
Don't defy me!

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.650
There's probably enough
for 100 meals in this.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.820
Bring it to your ship right away.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.310
--Owner Zeff!
--Owner Zeff!

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.720
Z... Zeff?

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:23.660
<i>"Protect Baratie!
The Great Pirate, Red Foot Zeff!"</i>

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.680
What're you doing?!
What're you thinking?!

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.980
If we revive even those on the ship,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.790
our restaurant will be
completely taken over!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:51.360
If they have the will to fight, that is...

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.350
...right, defeated warrior
of the Grand Line?

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.030
C... can't be...

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.700
Don Krieg is a defeated warrior...

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.740
Then even the ruler of
the East Blue couldn't...

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.310
Even the pirate fleet with
50 ships couldn't sail across...

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.300
Grand Line?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:18.650
Y... you must be Red Foot Zeff!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.720
So you are alive...

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.730
An incomparable pirate who was
a cook and yet also a captain...

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.630
So what if I'm alive?

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.330
It has nothing to do with you.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:38.000
As you can see, I live as a cook now.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.340
If you put it that way,
it sounds nice...

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.350
though rather than
living as a cook,

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.680
it looks like you can
live only as a cook.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:58.360
Red Foot Zeff was a master of kicks
who never used his hands in battle.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.630
I hear that his
strong legs crushed bedrock

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.370
and even left footprints on steel.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.970
And Red Foot referred to your shoes,
which were covered in the blood

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:13.300
that spattered as you
kicked your enemies down...

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:21.320
But you no longer have that
precious leg of yours...

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.850
I've heard the rumor...

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:27.660
How unlucky for you to have
an accident at sea...

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:34.660
To you, losing one of your legs
must mean you are unable to fight.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.000
What about fighting?

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
I can cook without a leg
as long as I have these hands.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.340
What're you trying to say?
Just come right out and say it!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.680
Red Foot Zeff.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.950
You're the man who once entered
the Grand Line and came back unhurt...

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.020
There should be a logbook
with the full year

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:02.290
of your journey chronicled in it...

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.950
Give that to me!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.300
Whoa! You've been to
the Grand Line, too, pops?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.300
Yeah...

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:16.970
My logbook, huh?
Indeed, I have it with me.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.640
But I can't give it to you.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.980
The logbook is the pride of all
the crewmen that I traveled with.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:30.990
It's too important to give it to you.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.320
Then, I'll just take
it from you by force.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.990
It's true that I fell
from the Grand Line.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:42.330
Even if that's the case, I'm still
Don Krieg, the strongest man.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.330
It's merely a dark sea route.
To sail across it, I had enough power...

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.000
and forces... as well as ambition!

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:55.080
The only thing that was regrettable
was that I lacked information.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.350
I just didn't know things...

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.020
I'll take your logbook.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:06.950
And I'll form a large pirate fleet
again and seize the One Piece.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:10.450
And then, I'll stand on top
in this Great Pirate Era!

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.300
Hold on a second!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.640
I'm the one who's gonna
be King of the Pirates!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.640
Chore boy!

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.980
Hey, back off, chore boy!
You're no match for him!

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.310
I can't back off on this.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:40.650
Did you say something, kid?

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.990
I can let it pass...

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:48.000
You don't have to.
I just stated a fact.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.430
This isn't a game.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:54.940
Of course not.
I'll conquer the Grand Line.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.770
It's no joke, you brat!

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:58.770
It's true that we didn't
have information,

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:01.010
but a fleet with 5000 men was
wiped out in just seven days!

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.780
That's a devilish sea!

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:05.280
There's no way someone like
you can sail across it!

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.110
S-seven days?!

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.620
Krieg's pirate ships were wiped
out in just seven days?!

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.950
What on earth happened?

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:17.620
Unfortunately, I don't find
those kinds of jokes funny.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.890
If you're not going to let it drop,

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.960
then how about
I just crush you here...

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.960
Go ahead if you can...

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.400
Fine by me.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:33.400
As you wish, I'll send
you to the netherworld.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.330
Gonna fight, Luffy?
Need a hand?

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:55.320
I-if you don't need help,
though, th-that's fine too...

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Zoro! Usopp! You stopped by?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.940
Don't worry. Just watch from there.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.440
Y-yeah? T-too bad,

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.610
but if you say so,
what can we do...

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:09.440
B-but if push comes to shove,
we'll help you.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.210
S-s-so, g-g-good luck!

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:14.620
What'd you do that for, Zoro?!

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.280
Shut up! Just keep quiet!

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.290
Are they your crewmembers?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.960
That's quite a small group you got!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.630
What're you saying?!
I've got two more!

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.290
Hey! You counted me, didn't you?!

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.140
I'll deal with you later.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.300
I'll go feed my underlings.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:51.650
Those who don't want to die can
abandon the restaurant and escape.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:56.650
All I'm after are
the logbook and this ship.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:04.000
But if you still wish
to be uselessly killed...

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.670
it's a bother, but I'll
bury you into the sea.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.330
Know that.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:28.020
It's gotten quiet.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:31.690
Big Bro Zoro went in there.
It should be all right.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:34.700
Hmm... Are they really okay, though?

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.530
If you put it that way...

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.700
Say, Big Sis Nami,
should we go in, too?

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:48.040
--Big Sis?!
--Ahhh! Ugh!

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.390
B-Big Sis Nami?

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:03.480
Hmm? Ahh, what is it?
Is something wrong?

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.170
<i>I'm sorry, Sanji-san.</i>

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:23.010
I never imagined this would happen...

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.710
That's not something you should
apologize for, underling.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:35.020
Each cook at this restaurant acted
as they felt was right. That's all.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:41.030
Owner! Why are you acting as
if you're taking Sanji's side?!

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:45.700
That's right! He's responsible
for this whole thing!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.700
He's going to put your precious
restaurant out of business!

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:51.710
Shut up, you idiots!

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:58.050
Have you felt what it's like to
be on the brink of starvation?!

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:03.320
Loosing food and water
on this grand ocean...

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:08.490
Do you know how scary it is?!
Do you know how hard it is?!

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:12.330
What?! What do you mean, Owner?

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.000
The difference between
Sanji and you all is

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.660
whether you know it or not.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:21.670
Hmm? What does he mean?

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.660
What's he saying that Sanji knows?

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:30.010
If you have time to grumble,

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:33.000
leave the restaurant from
the back door already!

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:38.020
I'll stay and fight.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:41.190
I couldn't bear it if I was
just beaten and didn't fight back.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.360
I'll stay, too! This is
the restaurant where I work!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.690
We don't have anywhere
else to go anyway!

00:12:55.370 --> 00:13:00.370
What do you think you're doing?!
You saw how powerful Don is, right?!

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.140
Hey, Ghin!

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:03.810
Let me tell you something.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:08.980
Feeding someone who's
hungry is my morality.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.140
But...

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.990
those we'll be dealing with
are plunderers with full bellies.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:23.760
I won't let you complain even when
I beat up your fellow pirates.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:26.000
If someone's going to
take over this restaurant,

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:30.000
even if it's you, I'll kill
them without hesitation!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.000
Got that?

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:38.680
Ha! Letting him live and now killing him?
You're hopeless, Sanji...

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.350
Shut up, you damn cook!

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.850
You see? He's kinda cool, isn't he?

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:45.190
Who cares about him!

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.350
We'd better get out of here now!

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:52.860
Calm down! Even if it's Krieg,
he's a wreck with injuries.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:57.460
Ghin! You said you didn't know
anything about the Grand Line.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.520
Even though you've been there?

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.380
It's still true that I don't know.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:12.710
What happened on the seventh day
after we entered the Grand Line...

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:17.120
I don't know if it
was a dream or reality...

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.950
I still haven't been able
to come to terms with it...

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:24.320
I still just can't believe...

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.590
that the 50-ship fleet...

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.000
was wiped out by only one man...

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:41.980
--What?!
--What?!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:07.300
It happened suddenly...

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:13.300
As soon as this man appeared,
he sank the ships one after another.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:20.980
If we hadn't been lucky enough
to have that storm then,

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:24.470
our main ship would've been
completely destroyed as well...

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:36.000
I don't know how many
ships we have left...

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.670
It was just so dreadful that I don't
want to accept it as reality...

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.670
I don't want to remember...

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.340
that man's...

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:52.350
sharp hawk-like eyes whose glare
alone gives one the chill of death.

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:53.680
Wha...

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.340
What did he just say?!

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:03.290
That...

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.630
must be Hawk-Eye...

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:07.960
What?

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:14.300
That you felt his eyes were like
a hawk's isn't proof in and of itself,

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:20.640
but what this man did is enough
proof that it's him...

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.310
Hawk-Eye!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.980
Huh? You know him, Zoro?

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:30.150
Yeah... He's the man I'm looking for.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.320
I went out to sea to meet him.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.320
I see...

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:39.330
Isn't it possible that that man had
some deep grudge towards you guys?

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.330
We never did anything to him!

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:44.000
Like you guys disturbed
his nap or something...

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.770
Don't be ridiculous!

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:50.340
I'll be damned if he crushed
our fleet for such a reason!

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:54.670
Don't get so worked up.
It's just an example.

00:16:54.670 --> 00:17:00.350
I'm just giving an example of what
kind of place the Grand Line is.

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.620
What the heck kind of place is that?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:06.620
It probably means that
anything can happen.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.620
Hey Luffy! Let's not
go to a place like that!

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:11.290
Luffy!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.800
Hey Luffy?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.130
Ahhh! It sounds so exciting!!

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:23.300
That's how it should be!

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:25.640
You need to get the concept of
"danger" into your thick skull!

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:30.640
But my goal is now completely
narrowed down to the Grand Line.

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.310
What?!

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:36.980
That man... I can see that
man if I go there...

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:41.320
Are you guys stupid or what?

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:43.990
Guys like you die before anyone else.

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:48.660
Yeah, but you didn't have
to call us "stupid."

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.530
When I decided to become
the strongest swordsman,

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.000
I decided to devote my life to it.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:59.000
Since it was my decision, the only
one who can call me stupid is me.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.780
Ahh! Me too, me too!

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:05.610
Me too! That's just natural
as a man of the sea!

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.440
In your case, that's a lie.

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.450
What nonsense...

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.960
Hey!

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:22.060
Do you idiots understand
the current situation?!

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.200
The ship moored in front
of the restaurant

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.230
is the huge Galleon that
belongs to Don Krieg,

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.140
Commodore of the "pirate fleet!"

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:31.300
If you wanna escape from reality,

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:33.640
do it after surviving
this life-or-death crisis!

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:47.650
--We're saved!!
--We're saved!!

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:49.320
Great! We're still alive!

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:50.820
It seems like a dream!

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.660
We're free from that nightmare!

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:58.000
We came back alive from
the pirate graveyard!

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:01.940
That's right...

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:06.430
which means that we can now
head to the Grand Line again.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:12.610
Huh? What's with those faces?

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:16.010
A-are we going to that place again?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:26.220
No more objections, right?

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:42.310
First, abandon this wrecked ship
that could sink at any moment

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:44.310
and take over the restaurant.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:47.550
Our enemy's just some punk cooks.

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:51.540
Even if you take your opponent lightly,
that's still more than enough...

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.830
Attack!

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.100
Here they come!
We can hear their war cry!

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.440
We'll protect the ship to the end!
It's our restaurant!

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.510
Out of our way, cooks!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.370
What the?!

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.370
What happened?!

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:49.710
Don Krieg!

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:53.380
The main ship was... cut!

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.380
Cut?! It was cut, you said?!

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.990
This huge Galleon was?!

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:04.980
That can't be true!!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:15.670
Raise the anchor! Or we'll be
swallowed along with the ship!

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.000
Yes sir!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:23.170
This is bad! Nami, Yosaku and Johnny
are still on our ship out there!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:27.010
Dammit! It might be too late!

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:39.360
Big Bro! Big Bro!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:42.200
Yosaku! Johnny!

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.360
Are you all right?

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.200
Where's the ship?! It's gone!
What happened to Nami?!

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:51.040
That... I'm sorry,
Big Bro. She's gone.

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:53.770
See ya! Tell them...

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:55.440
Big Sis Nami...

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:58.710
that if we're linked by fate,
we'll meet again.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:02.650
She took all the treasure
and ran off!

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:06.020
<i>--Wh-what'd you say?!
--Wh-what'd you say?!</i>

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:19.990
That man is...

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:37.340
Th-that son of a bitch!
He followed us!

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:52.870
Is it possible... that's...

00:22:52.870 --> 00:22:54.970
...Hawk-Eye!

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:06.070
<i>When I was little, I had
a vision of a treasure map</i>

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:17.220
<i>and I always searched
for that miraculous place</i>

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:24.390
<i>before someone else could
beat me to it</i>

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:37.000
<i>If the world is going to change</i>

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:45.490
<i>before I can even attain my dream</i>

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:52.560
<i>then take me to the time
when I knew nothing</i>

00:23:52.560 --> 00:24:02.560
<i>so that my memories won't fade</i>
